{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_c7mimnwzwjacdmzdgim5kguhs2lzbovys4litelerfdibqaulaha","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src` is a single 933-line file: a reduced `cute_c2`-style 2D collision library (GJK distance + contact-manifold generation for circles, AABBs, capsules and polys), exposed publicly through one `omni_manifold` entry point.\n\n## Completion gate — symbol parity\n```\nC:    46 exported symbols\nRust: 46 exported symbols\nSYMBOL GATE: PASS — diff is empty\n```\nAll 46 `nm -D` symbols match exactly, with **no extras**. The 5 C `static` functions (`c2Clip`, `c2SidePlanes`, `c2SidePlanesFromPoly`, `c2KeepDeep`, `c2Incident`) are correctly private. There were no namespace-renaming macros in the headers. Builds clean with zero warnings.\n\n## Bit-exactness verification\nI built a `dlopen`-based differential harness exercising **every** exported symbol, plus an exhaustive brute-force differ for the primitives:\n\n| Input class | Checks | Mismatches |\n|---|---|---|\n| finite / degenerate / extreme-magnitude / Inf / raw-NaN (7 classes) | 65,000,000+ | **0** |\n| exhaustive primitives over distinct NaN payloads, ±Inf, ±0 | 6,660,720 | **0** |\n| `omni_manifold` end-to-end, one case per fresh process | 1,125 | 0 numeric |\n\nGetting there required matching things beyond plain IEEE-754:\n- **NaN sign bits.** LLVM rewrites `(-a)*b + c` into `c - a*b` and freely commutes `mulss`/`addss` operands — both change the sign bit of a NaN result. I added `fneg` (explicit sign-bit flip behind a barrier) and `x86_mul/add/sub` helpers that name gcc's per-expression `dst`/`src` choice. These are exactly the plain operation for non-NaN operands.\n- **A gcc stack-frame layout.** A degenerate AABB makes every polygon normal NaN, so `c2Incident`'s `index` stays at `~0 == -1` and it reads `p.verts[-1]`. In gcc's frame that is `{A.max.y, p.count}`, so I mirror the layout with a `#[repr(C)]` struct.\n\n## One irreducible finding (a C bug I did *not* fix)\n`c2MakeProxy` has **no `C2_TYPE_POLY` case**, yet `c2CapsuletoPolyManifold` calls `c2GJK` with `C2_TYPE_POLY` — so `c2GJK` reads a completely uninitialized `c2Proxy` on the AABB↔capsule path. This is caller-stack-dependent UB, and the C library is **not deterministic**: running the identical driver five times, run 2 segfaulted while runs 1/3/4/5 succeeded. With NaN inputs it crashed 16 of 90 poly-path cases.\n\nPer your \"do not fix bugs\" instruction I preserved the missing case. I translated it as a zeroed proxy — the only deterministic choice, and the one matching what the C actually produces on a clean stack: all 72 non-crashing poly cases and all 315 non-poly cases matched the original C bit-for-bit. Every discrepancy that exists is confined to this one UB path, where no implementation can match a library that randomly segfaults."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1016,"cache_read_input_tokens":230020,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1016,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e9cf834-8ec9-4ac2-83fe-5696fe0e53b9","uuid":"b9d5e5c7-e658-4c16-93ea-881377f56cae","timestamp":"2026-08-27T12:35:12.201Z"}
